{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/17943-need-an-st-for-online-game-please-help","id":17943,"title":"Need an ST for online game, please help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-25T14:54:19-08:00","id":17943,"title":"Need an ST for online game, please help","content":"Hi there,<br /> <br /> I'm just now crossing over from the old WW forums. I rarely posted there and mainly hung around on the Onyx Path updates and made comments. Lately with all the 20th anniversary work I've found more and more to talk about. The old forums were a good information resource for me, but had too much of an all boys club feel for me whenever I spoke up. In fact I'm not even sure this is the correct section to be asking this, but what the hey. I've been an online player for a long time and gradually the online chat rooms went the way of C-WoD itself and now most of the online chat games have privatized into their own themes and systems. I personally have a small group of individuals I run small scenes with over emails, google docs or IMs. Something I've discovered, I suck at being an ST in some ways. I just don't have a head for running combat scenes. I can work up a story, handle intrigue and character development, that kind of thing. The way we play is more Role Play than Roll Play, but die use throws in that exciting unknown element into it. Wall-o-text novella type scenes that get pretty dynamic and have system crossovers. However there's the issue of combat. We've had a long running campaign that needs more direct conflicts. When the story requires it, it's a hit or miss with the numbers. I need help. I need an ST willing to run a few scenes for me and a couple other people. Maybe even just two of us. Mainly I need someone who is willing to run a few werewolf scenes with enemies. Someone who isn't afraid of crossovers or can 